WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.954
An ordinary three D model shows you an object.

2
00:00:03.105 --> 00:00:05.183
A demonstration shows you how it works.

3
00:00:05.357 --> 00:00:07.645
Interaction Twin connects the two.

4
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.987
Record an everyday interaction, and turn it into a source-linked object

5
00:00:13.022 --> 00:00:16.552
program: the parts, their connections, and what happened.

6
00:00:16.877 --> 00:00:20.534
Your agent can inspect that knowledge, follow its evidence, and reuse

7
00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:21.196
it.

8
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.798
Combine a phone and charger from separate recordings.

9
00:00:29.007 --> 00:00:32.676
Describe a new task, then rehearse it in three D before physical

10
00:00:32.734 --> 00:00:33.488
validation.

11
00:00:41.073 --> 00:00:42.501
Show an interaction once.

12
00:00:42.652 --> 00:00:44.300
Keep how it works.

13
00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:49.127
The library turns recorded demonstrations into objects you can explore.

14
00:00:49.452 --> 00:00:53.550
Compare source video with connected replay, inspect individual parts,

15
00:00:53.573 --> 00:00:56.185
and download geometry and descriptive files.

16
00:00:56.627 --> 00:00:59.053
Every example keeps its evidence close.

17
00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.017
An object program adds meaning to geometry.

18
00:01:06.261 --> 00:01:10.452
It describes which parts belong together, which relationships are estimated,

19
00:01:10.521 --> 00:01:12.216
and which actions were observed.

20
00:01:12.425 --> 00:01:16.175
Source references are preserved, while unknown physical properties stay

21
00:01:16.233 --> 00:01:17.092
explicit.

22
00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.856
Muse proposes the structure.

23
00:01:23.181 --> 00:01:27.059
Separate prompts ask the same model to critique it alongside code checks.

24
00:01:27.233 --> 00:01:30.867
Repairs can follow, before the owner approves the exact revision.

25
00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:39.259
That knowledge reaches an agent through a local, read-only M C P

26
00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:42.916
server. The agent can search, inspect interfaces, retrieve

27
00:01:42.951 --> 00:01:45.424
geometry, and follow source evidence.

28
00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.425
The phone and charger make reuse concrete.

29
00:01:50.668 --> 00:01:54.511
A saved client inspected two recordings and prepared a shared task draft.

30
00:01:54.755 --> 00:01:58.064
Those interface matches are candidates; compatibility still needs

31
00:01:58.110 --> 00:01:59.771
independent validation.

32
00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:05.951
The preview makes a proposed task easier to inspect.

33
00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:09.167
The case and earbuds become a complete, editable rehearsal.

34
00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:12.057
The source recording remains available for comparison.

35
00:02:12.336 --> 00:02:15.761
Then the same approach brings the phone and charger into one scene.

36
00:02:16.364 --> 00:02:20.509
These authored kinematics communicate an idea before contact, insertion,

37
00:02:20.625 --> 00:02:23.365
and hardware execution are validated.

38
00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:34.120
Meta's models provide perception and proposals: Muse for structure,

39
00:02:34.294 --> 00:02:38.322
SAM for segmentation, and SAM three D for component drafts.

40
00:02:38.833 --> 00:02:42.955
Our code builds source-linked object programs, manages checks, review

41
00:02:43.002 --> 00:02:46.403
and approval, and exposes the results through viewers and M C

42
00:02:46.531 --> 00:02:47.622
P.

43
00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:51.483
The next step is physical validation.

44
00:02:51.657 --> 00:02:55.616
The foundation is inspectable: real demonstrations, reusable

45
00:02:55.662 --> 00:02:58.031
object knowledge. Interaction Twin.
